  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nRidging overhead, combined with a warm southwest flow in place\ntoday as resulted in temperatures soaring into the 70s for most\nof the area. Near-record high temperatures are expected this\nafternoon. The warm temperatures are expected to remain in place\ntonight. In fact, tonight's forecast low temperatures (mid 50s\nto near 60 degrees) are several degrees warmer than the normal\nhigh temperatures for this time of the year.\n\nAnother warm day is expected on Thursday with highs in the upper\n60s to lower 70s for most of the area. This is expected to be\nthe case despite the cloud cover and scattered rain showers\nahead of an approaching cold front.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nThe aforementioned cold front will move through the region on\nThursday, which will bring rain showers to the area, especially\nin the morning. This frontal passage continues to trend a bit\nfaster and therefore the afternoon may actually end up being\nmainly dry aside from some isolated lingering light rain\nshowers. Partial clearing is also expected in the afternoon. \n\nMost of the area should stay dry Friday, with possibly showers \ncontinuing across the Poconos and southern Catskills as a wave \nof low pressure tracks along the Mid Atlantic Coast. Shower \npotential will increase again Saturday morning from west to \neast, as the upper level low tracks into the area and slowly \npushes through, with isolated to scattered showers lingering \nuntil Sunday morning.\n\nAnother trough dropping southeast out of Canada will bring \nanother chance for showers late Sunday night into Monday, with \nlake enhancement adding to the shower potential.",
